[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4892136632","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120976#issuecomment-4892136632","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120976","id":4892136632,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI5gUuA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T11:14:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T11:15:36Z","body":"> The first pass only clears static variables, and ensures that correct user code does receive NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE\r\n> The second pass cancels all pending functions and partially destructs remaining instances. Both of those are user errors at this point so no one gets notified about anything.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand this order. Shouldn't static variables be cleared after all `NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE`s and canceling pending functions?\r\n\r\n> I did play through the first few levels of Rift Riff\r\n\r\nNice! :D ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4892136632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4892393170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120976#issuecomment-4892393170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120976","id":4892393170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI5v-0g","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T11:44:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T11:44:58Z","body":"> I'm not sure I understand this order. Shouldn't static variables be cleared after all `NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE`s and canceling pending functions?\r\n\r\nThis is about ensuring that `RefCounted` objects that are stored in static variables do receive `NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE`. So clearing the static variables of the script leads to their values receiving the notification.\r\n\r\nFor core types this would not be an issue. But if the ref counted value has a script 